{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FxPAeLXK6dkw2VPxTosVQ5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"ARR SAC Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/sacguidelines\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about ACL Rolling Review (ARR) reviewer guidelines, review form, and scoring rubric for 2025-2026:\n\n## Scoring System\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. The soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\n## Key Guidelines\n\nPersonal preferences are more subjective and should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper. If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\n## Review Quality Standards\n\nThe program chairs and ARR EiCs will consider egregious cases reported by chairs, including the cases of extremely terse reviews, unprofessional tone, and LLM-generated reviews. The 'highly irresponsible' reviewers or chairs may have their work desk-rejected from the current cycle, and ineligible for resubmission or commitment during the following ARR cycle.\n\n## Recognition Program\n\nStarting from May 2025, ACL introduces the awards policy for reviewers & chairs. In short, the area chairs or senior area chairs may nominate the great reviewers, and senior chairs may also nominate area chairs who perform great service.\n\nThe full reviewer guidelines and review form can be accessed at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines and http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform respectively.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b278507-b3d6-452e-b8e4-ad54eb721597","uuid":"3975dcbf-84fe-4352-8649-f041b73d2e24","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:48:40.564Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric 2025 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01JeVLxX4MvKLAFKKNJxVgwC","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"ARR SAC Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/sacguidelines"}]},"Based on the web search results, here's what I found about ACL Rolling Review (ARR) reviewer guidelines, review form, and scoring rubric for 2025-2026:\n\n## Scoring System\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. The soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\n## Key Guidelines\n\nPersonal preferences are more subjective and should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper. If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\n## Review Quality Standards\n\nThe program chairs and ARR EiCs will consider egregious cases reported by chairs, including the cases of extremely terse reviews, unprofessional tone, and LLM-generated reviews. The 'highly irresponsible' reviewers or chairs may have their work desk-rejected from the current cycle, and ineligible for resubmission or commitment during the following ARR cycle.\n\n## Recognition Program\n\nStarting from May 2025, ACL introduces the awards policy for reviewers & chairs. In short, the area chairs or senior area chairs may nominate the great reviewers, and senior chairs may also nominate area chairs who perform great service.\n\nThe full reviewer guidelines and review form can be accessed at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines and http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform respectively."],"durationSeconds":7.4404271560000055}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TFthhvzYNyD6faT5y7ivZg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 acceptance rate review criteria dimensions\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Decisions: Community Insights and the Controversial Desk Rejections | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/131/emnlp-2025-decisions-community-insights-and-the-controversial-desk-rejections\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Main Conference Papers - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/calls/main_conference_papers/\"},{\"title\":\"Jan. 2025 ACL Standing Committee on Peer Review (COPR) Report 1\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/9/9e/COPR-5-cycle-report-to-publish.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Conference Decisions · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://gist.github.com/antonisa/2158dee79179c7c49304ef353887bfa0\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP Acceptance Rates and Submission Stats - OpenAccept\",\"url\":\"https://openaccept.org/c/ai/emnlp/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Industry Track | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FIndustry_Track\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP/2025\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about EMNLP 2025:\n\n## Acceptance Rate\n\nThe EMNLP 2025 Main acceptance rate was just over 22%.\n\n## Review Criteria and Dimensions\n\nAccording to the review process, papers are evaluated using multiple criteria including the reviews (reflected by both the actual text and the soundness and excitement scores), the rebuttal and/or discussion with authors, the recommendation from the Area Chair, the Senior Area Chair's own reading of the papers, thematic diversity considerations, and the Senior Area Chair's own views on what constitutes publication-worthy material.\n\nThe ranking system used for *ACL conferences is: Accept-Main, Borderline-Main-Findings, Accept-Findings, Borderline-Findings-Reject, and Reject.\n\n## Reviewer Policies\n\nThe criteria for \"highly irresponsible\" reviewing covers the non-submission of (meta-)reviews on time without due warning, extremely terse reviews for good-faith submissions, and egregious cases of unprofessional tone and LLM policy violations. 82 papers were desk-rejected because at least one author had been identified as an irresponsible reviewer, marking a notable policy change at EMNLP 2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b278507-b3d6-452e-b8e4-ad54eb721597","uuid":"4bfe49a6-1519-4dbe-bb86-67be49cf63f2","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:48:41.314Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 acceptance rate review criteria dimensions","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Sd8M9yxqwH9dbyMd5Vhjvi","content":[{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Decisions: Community Insights and the Controversial Desk Rejections | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/131/emnlp-2025-decisions-community-insights-and-the-controversial-desk-rejections"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"EMNLP Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/"},{"title":"Call for Main Conference Papers - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/calls/main_conference_papers/"},{"title":"Jan. 2025 ACL Standing Committee on Peer Review (COPR) Report 1","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/9/9e/COPR-5-cycle-report-to-publish.pdf"},{"title":"Conference Decisions · GitHub","url":"https://gist.github.com/antonisa/2158dee79179c7c49304ef353887bfa0"},{"title":"EMNLP Acceptance Rates and Submission Stats - OpenAccept","url":"https://openaccept.org/c/ai/emnlp/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Industry Track | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FIndustry_Track"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP/2025"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about EMNLP 2025:\n\n## Acceptance Rate\n\nThe EMNLP 2025 Main acceptance rate was just over 22%.\n\n## Review Criteria and Dimensions\n\nAccording to the review process, papers are evaluated using multiple criteria including the reviews (reflected by both the actual text and the soundness and excitement scores), the rebuttal and/or discussion with authors, the recommendation from the Area Chair, the Senior Area Chair's own reading of the papers, thematic diversity considerations, and the Senior Area Chair's own views on what constitutes publication-worthy material.\n\nThe ranking system used for *ACL conferences is: Accept-Main, Borderline-Main-Findings, Accept-Findings, Borderline-Findings-Reject, and Reject.\n\n## Reviewer Policies\n\nThe criteria for \"highly irresponsible\" reviewing covers the non-submission of (meta-)reviews on time without due warning, extremely terse reviews for good-faith submissions, and egregious cases of unprofessional tone and LLM policy violations. 82 papers were desk-rejected because at least one author had been identified as an irresponsible reviewer, marking a notable policy change at EMNLP 2025."],"durationSeconds":7.737285734999998}}
